00:03:18,620 --> 00:03:24,620
Change is in the air.

2
00:06:37,241 --> 00:06:43,241
Up is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Pete Docter.

3
00:09:55,862 --> 00:10:01,862
Carl Fredricksen spent his entire life dreaming of exploring
the globe and experiencing life to its fullest.

4
00:13:14,482 --> 00:13:20,482
But at age 78, life seems to have passed him by, until a twist of fate (and a persistent
8-year old Wilderness Explorer named Russell) gives him a new lease on life.

5
00:16:33,103 --> 00:16:39,103
Carl Fredricksen (voice), played by Ed Asner.

6
00:19:51,724 --> 00:19:57,724
Charles F. Muntz (voice), played by Christopher Plummer.

7
00:23:10,344 --> 00:23:16,344
Russell (voice), played by Jordan Nagai.

8
00:26:28,965 --> 00:26:34,965
Dug / Alpha (voice), played by Bob Peterson.

9
00:29:47,586 --> 00:29:53,586
Beta (voice), played by Delroy Lindo.

10
00:33:06,206 --> 00:33:12,206
Gamma (voice), played by Jerome Ranft.

11
00:36:24,827 --> 00:36:30,827
Up is a 2009 American animated adventure comedy-drama film directed by
Pete Docter and written by Bob Peterson and Docter.

12
00:39:43,448 --> 00:39:49,448
Produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures, the film centers on Carl Fredricksen (voiced by Ed Asner), an elderly widower who, by attaching several helium
balloons to his house, travels to South America with youngster Russell (voiced by Jordan Nagai) in order to fulfill a promise that he made to his late wife.

13
00:43:02,068 --> 00:43:08,068
Along the way, they befriend a talking dog (voiced by Peterson) as well as an exotic bird and encounter Carl's
childhood idol (voiced by Christopher Plummer), who has sinister plans to capture the bird.

14
00:46:20,689 --> 00:46:26,689
Originally titled Heliums, Docter conceived the outline for Up in 2004 based on
fantasies of escaping from life when it became too irritating.

15
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:45,310
He and eleven other Pixar artists spent three days in
Venezuela for research and inspiration.

16
00:52:57,931 --> 00:53:03,931
The designs of the characters were caricatured and stylized considerably,
and animators were challenged with creating realistic cloth.

17
00:56:16,551 --> 00:56:22,551
Composer Michael Giacchino composed the film's score.

18
00:59:35,172 --> 00:59:41,172
It was Pixar's first film to be presented in 3D format.

19
01:02:53,793 --> 01:02:59,793
Up debuted at the 62nd Cannes Film Festival on May 13, 2009,
and was released in the United States on May 29.

20
01:06:12,413 --> 01:06:18,413
It received critical acclaim for its screenplay, animation, characters, themes, narrative, emotional
depth, humor, Asner's performance, Giacchino's musical score and its opening montage.

21
01:09:31,034 --> 01:09:37,034
The National Board of Review and the American Film Institute
named Up one of the top-ten films of 2009.

22
01:12:49,655 --> 01:12:55,655
Up earned $735.1 million worldwide, finishing its theatrical
run as the sixth-highest-grossing film of 2009.

23
01:16:08,275 --> 01:16:14,275
It was nominated for five awards at the 82nd Academy Awards,
winning two, and received numerous other accolades.

24
01:19:26,896 --> 01:19:32,896
Among its Academy Award nominations, it became the second of three animated films ever to receive a nomination for the Academy Award for
Best Picture (after 1991's Beauty and the Beast and before 2010's Toy Story 3), ultimately losing to The Hurt Locker.

25
01:22:45,517 --> 01:22:51,517
Since then, it has been and continues to be regarded as one of the
greatest animated films of the 21st century and of all time.

26
01:26:04,137 --> 01:26:10,137
A short-form sequel series, Dug Days, premiered on Disney+ on September 1, 2021.

27
01:29:22,758 --> 01:29:28,758
The film explores themes of central and south america,
age difference, villain, balloon, travel.

28
01:32:41,379 --> 01:32:47,379
The tone is lighthearted and mind_bending.
